  ('p','**How does an evacuation sled for stairs work?**'),
  ('p','The person is placed on the Ulti-Mat, the side wings are wrapped around them, and the straps are fastened. Two staff members then pull the mat by its head and foot straps, sliding it across the floor and down the stairs without lifting the person.'),
  ('p','**How many people does it take to use the Ulti-Mat?**'),
  ('p','Two. The long pulling straps at the head and feet let more people help when needed.'),
  ('p','**What is the difference between the standard and bariatric Ulti-Mat?**'),
